- PARTLY DONE (2026-08-10) Give field types (e.g., string, bool, float) to the LLM during the prompting and explicitly ask it to cast variables that need to if using CEL.
  Types were ALREADY given, in training and evaluation, and correct for all 42 attribute filters.
  The real defect was VALUES: training rendered `Status (String: full, empty)` in 5,910 prompts,
  evaluation rendered `Status (String)` - so the model was taught to read literals like "0",
  "Flagged", "3" off the prompt and then denied them. Fixed: LogEvents collects distinct values
  for string attributes (cap 10), build_schema_block renders them, and an EVENT ATTRIBUTES
  section makes 03_hiring's Decision/Outcome/Result visible (6 filters that were previously
  unanswerable). Numeric ranges were considered and rejected - every numeric literal in the
  testset comes from the question text. Still open: CEL casting guidance (2 entries need the
  prefix `int(o1.attr(...))` form, which appears 0 times in training).
  See Thesis/notes/11-evaluation-readiness.md 6.5.
